- Do NOT click "Create promotion" until step 6 explicitly says to.
- If a modal fails to open after clicking Edit, wait 3s, scroll to make section visible, click Edit again ONCE.

CAMPAIGN: TODC-1209-$30 | STORE: 1209 (McDonald's (1209-DES PERES)) | SUBTOTAL: $30 | TAGS: 14, 20, 27, 29, 33, 34, 35, 42

STEP 1 — Open campaign builder:
- Click "Marketing" in the left sidebar. Wait for page to load.
- Click "Run a campaign". Wait for campaign type cards.
- Find "Discount for all customers" card, click "Select".
- Click "Customize your campaign" in the right panel. Wait for form to load.

STEP 2 — Select store:
- Click Edit (pencil) next to "Stores". Wait for modal.
- Click "Select All" to deselect all stores.
- Search "1209" in search bar. If found, select it. If NOT found, search "McDonald's (1209-DES PERES)" instead.
- Select ONLY the one matching store. Click "Save".

STEP 3 — Set customer incentive:
- Click Edit (pencil) next to "Customer incentive". Wait for modal.
- Click "15%" radio button.
- Click "Custom" under Minimum subtotal. Click the input field.
- Select all text (triple-click), type: 30
- Wait 2s. VERIFY field shows 30 or $30. If it shows $25 or wrong value, clear and retype.
- Click LEFTMOST button under "Maximum discount amount" (smallest value).
- Click "Save".

STEP 4 — Set schedule:
- Click Edit (pencil) next to "Scheduling". Wait for modal with grid.
- Click "Set a custom schedule". Wait for grid.
- Grid: 6 rows (Early morning, Breakfast, Lunch, Afternoon, Dinner, Late night) x 7 cols (Mon-Sun).
- The grid opens with ALL 42 cells selected. We need only 8 specific cells.
- FIRST: Click "Weekdays" ONCE to deselect weekday cells.
- THEN: Click "Weekends" ONCE to deselect weekend cells.
- Now the grid should be empty. Do NOT click "Weekdays" or "Weekends" again.
- SELECT these 8 cells by clicking each ONCE:
  - Breakfast row: click Sun
  - Lunch row: click Sat
  - Afternoon row: click Sat
  - Dinner row: click Mon, Fri, Sat, Sun
  - Late night row: click Sun
- After clicking all 8 cells above, click "Save" immediately.
- Do NOT re-check or verify the grid. Do NOT click any cell a second time. Do NOT click "Weekdays" or "Weekends" again.

STEP 5 — Set campaign name:
- Click Edit (pencil) next to "Campaign name".
- Clear all text, type exactly: TODC-1209-$30
- Click "Save".

STEP 6 — Final verify and create:
- BEFORE clicking "Create promotion", read the campaign summary panel:
  - Confirm it shows "$30" (not $25 unless target is $25). If wrong, click Edit next to "Customer incentive", fix it, Save.
  - Confirm campaign name shows "TODC-1209-$30".
- Click "Create promotion". Wait for success confirmation.
- IMPORTANT: If you see a message like "The details of this campaign are the same as one of your live campaigns" or any duplication warning, do NOT try to fix it. Just use the done action immediately and say: "TODC-1209-$30" DUPLICATE for store 1209.

